WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.550
Last year, Boston 311 took

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:04.100
300,000 requests.

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:07.500
In Transportation, half of them ran late.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:09.900
So picture New Year's Eve, 2025.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:12.300
Did your crews miss again?

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:15.100
This is Bat-Terry.

00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.650
Give Terry a goal,

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:18.600
he flips it into how it would fail.

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:20.100
It finds your way out.

00:00:20.450 --> 00:00:22.400
Here's one such goal.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.200
Every department closes 95%

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.400
of its requests on time, all year.

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.800
Terry flips it into a failure,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.400
then listens for predators.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.200
That is, specific ways this goal could fail.

00:00:35.650 --> 00:00:36.850
Each one checked against

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:38.600
Boston's 2024 records.

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.000
Some are confirmed, some rejected.

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:44.950
Terry finds the cheapest escape.

00:00:45.450 --> 00:00:47.000
Public Works falls short,

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.500
so Terry signs four crews by the end of June,

00:00:49.800 --> 00:00:51.000
working from August.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:55.500
$260,000 in payroll for 96% on time.

00:00:57.050 --> 00:00:59.100
And you can ask what-ifs in plain words.

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:00.900
A windstorm in June?

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.300
Terry answers live,

00:01:02.350 --> 00:01:04.100
and every number comes from the engine.

00:01:06.950 --> 00:01:09.400
Residents report problems in their own words,

00:01:09.450 --> 00:01:10.900
even in Spanish.

00:01:11.250 --> 00:01:12.850
Terry asks which Centre Street,

00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:14.900
then routes it to Pothole Repair.

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:17.400
On 200 unseen messages,

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:20.600
it was right 82.5% of the time.

00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:22.750
Under Terry is a real plan.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:25.100
We tested four forecasts on 2024,

00:01:25.850 --> 00:01:27.300
kept the most accurate,

00:01:27.350 --> 00:01:31.000
and planned for demand 14% above or below it.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:35.100
The plan costs 15.62 million dollars,

00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:38.950
6.19 million less than keeping January's crews.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:41.900
The biggest decision:

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.800
Transportation signs six crews by New Year's Eve.

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:50.200
Three years of 311 records become a forecast

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:53.500
and a crew simulator that runs in your browser.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.300
Your goal goes through one Netlify function,

00:01:56.350 --> 00:02:00.200
which guards the key to GPT-6.1 Sol.

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:02.500
The model calls our engine as a tool

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:03.900
and writes one sentence,

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.500
and a guardrail checks every number.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.600
We tested it against a broken model

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:10.600
and 200 random actions.

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:12.000
And then comes the map,

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:13.900
which we call the Echolocation,

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.550
which shows quiet neighborhoods

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:17.300
are not the slow ones.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:20.900
So what makes Bat-Terry different?

00:02:21.400 --> 00:02:22.600
Most tools plan forward.

00:02:23.200 --> 00:02:26.000
Terry starts from the day the goal fails, and works back.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:29.600
Every risk it raises is tested on 2024,

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:32.000
so nothing rests on a hunch.

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:34.100
The math is ours.

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:36.300
The model only explains it,

00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:38.200
and a guardrail checks every figure.

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:40.900
A resident's message, in their own words,

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:43.000
lands with the crew that fixes it.

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:46.900
And if a goal can't be met in time,

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.600
Terry says so, instead of pretending.

00:02:50.050 --> 00:02:51.200
That's Bat-Terry.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.100
Every plan tested against failure,

00:02:53.150 --> 00:02:55.000
before Boston has to live with it.
